# NOTES #

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Bulgaria#cite_ref-5]  Bulgarian election law permits voters to vote against all candidates. In reality, this has no effect, as those votes aren't counted during the tally and as such would not affect the outcome of the election.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Bulgaria#cite_ref-10]  Revocation of citizenship can only be done to citizens who acquired their citizenship through the process of  [LINK: (naturalization) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naturalization]  and not to native-born Bulgarians.

It can only be applied after the citizen in question has been convicted of a serious crime and even then cannot be performed if the revocation would cause the person to enter into  [LINK: (statelessness) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statelessness]  (i.e. has no other citizenship).

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Bulgaria#cite_ref-11]  In practice this power is very weak, as after a veto the bill is sent back to the assembly for another vote, in which the veto can be overruled by a simple majority. If the veto is overruled, the President is constitutionally obliged to sign the bill into law.


